{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): sorry, uh, the bus was a mess and I almost turned around. my stomach's in knots about coming.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. one sec, this screen's doing that thing again. okay. what are we seeing you for.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (PATIENT): it's my heel. um it hurts so bad on the first steps in the morning. been going on two months.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. wrong chart, hang on. say that again? which side, and how long.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (PATIENT): the right. right heel. two months. first steps in the morning, soon as my foot hits the floor.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (CAREGIVER): she's been limping around the apartment every morning. I hear it from the kitchen.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): you on your feet for work?",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (PATIENT): yeah, checkout at the market. eight hour shifts, sometimes more. and I run, well I try, three mornings a week. or I did, before all this.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (PATIENT): oh, and shoes. I got new running shoes, uh, about six weeks back? well actually the clogs came first, the old ones split, then the runners.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (CAREGIVER): and her sister keeps leaving biotin. the sister takes it for her hair. whole bottle on our counter. I told her that's not hers.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (PATIENT): but should I take it, the biotin? is my heel a vitamin thing? I was up googling stress fractures and now I'm sure it's cracked. or, I don't know, something bad.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): sorry, the cursor jumped. biotin's your sister's, ignore that. say the pain part again, does it ease or is it there all day.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (PATIENT): it eases, yeah. I walk around the kitchen, maybe ten minutes, and it backs off. then I'm on the register the whole shift and it comes right back. like a stab, under the heel.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): let me press here. tender right at the bottom, medial side of that right heel. no swelling I can see.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): any fever with this?",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (PATIENT): no. no fever.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): how about the respiratory stuff, breathing, cough, chest, any of that?",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): no. that whole thing is fine.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): weight. you dropping or putting it on?",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (PATIENT): err, umm, I don't know. I don't own a scale. my jeans fit, I think. or maybe they're a little looser, I really can't say.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): alright. I'm gonna order an x-ray of the heel and start naproxen, 500 milligrams twice a day with food.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (PATIENT): an x-ray, so you think it's broken? and naproxen, that's gonna mess my stomach up, right? how many weeks am I on it? and can I still run or am I gonna snap something?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (CAREGIVER): she already tried that. the naproxin, the aleve. last month. two pills and she was up all night with heartburn. quit after three days.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (PATIENT): yeah, I should've said, sorry. the heartburn was awful. I'm not taking that again. and those new running shoes, they pinch right on the heel. I only got them on twice.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): okay, forget the naproxen then. and actually hold the x-ray. first-step pain, tender where I pressed, shoes pinching, I don't need films. no tests today.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): plan is calf stretches, both legs, morning and before your shift, and a pair of cushioned insoles. drugstore ones are fine, in the work shoes.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (PATIENT): thirty seconds or what? am I headed for surgery? what if the insoles don't do a thing? is this that plantar, um, fasciitis?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): thirty seconds, three times a side, knee straight then knee bent. not surgery. this behaves like plantar fasciitis. that's my working read, not something a scan has proved.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (PATIENT): can I run at all? I'm scared to even jog to the corner.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): ease off the running for now. walk if those first steps calm down. if you're still hobbling in about four weeks, come back and we'll rethink.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I'll put the stretches on the fridge. she forgets stuff when she's wound up.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (PATIENT): so no biotin, for sure? and which insoles, superfeet or the cheap ones? if four weeks isn't enough do I call or just walk in?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): skip the biotin, that's your sister's supplement, it doesn't do anything for a heel. any cushioned insole, don't overthink the brand.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. if it's not better you come back, about four weeks, like I said. I gotta get this note in before the computer kicks me out."
 ],
